# Cases surfaced by differential testing against alacritty_terminal 0.26.0,
# proposed for promotion to spec/core/.

=== IL resets the cursor column to the first column
size 6x3
input "111111\r\n222222\e[2;4H\e[LX"
screen
  |111111|
  |X     |
  |222222|
cursor 2,2
ref DEC STD 070 (IL moves to column 1; xterm matches, ECMA-48 8.3.67 and alacritty_terminal keep the column)

=== DL resets the cursor column to the first column
size 6x3
input "111111\r\n222222\r\n333333\e[2;4H\e[MX"
screen
  |111111|
  |X33333|
  |      |
cursor 2,2
ref DEC STD 070 (DL moves to column 1; xterm matches, ECMA-48 8.3.32 and alacritty_terminal keep the column)

=== CBT cancels a pending wrap and moves to the previous tab stop
size 10x2
input "abcdefghij\e[ZX"
screen
  |abcdefghXj|
  |          |
cursor 10,1
ref ctlseqs: CSI Ps Z (CBT); tmux cancels pending wrap, while xterm and alacritty_terminal keep it

=== Mode 1049 reset on the main screen restores the saved cursor
size 8x2
input "\e[2;4H\e7\e[1;1Habc\e[?1049lX"
screen
  |abc     |
  |   X    |
cursor 5,2
ref ctlseqs: CSI ? 1049 l (combines mode 1047 reset and DECRC; xterm matches, alacritty_terminal ignores it on the main screen)

=== Mode 1049 set on the alternate screen saves the cursor
size 8x2
input "\e[?1049h\e[2;4H\e[?1049h\e[1;1Habc\e8X"
screen
  |abc     |
  |   X    |
cursor 5,2
ref ctlseqs: CSI ? 1049 h (combines DECSC and mode 1047 set; xterm matches, alacritty_terminal ignores it on the alternate screen)

=== A combining character at the first column without a preceding character is dropped
size 6x2
input "\u0301\e[CX"
screen
  | X    |
  |      |
cursor 3,1
ref docs/design/emulation.md section 7.2 (xterm -u8 drops combining marks on blank cells; alacritty_terminal attaches them to a space)

=== EL 0, 1, and 2 cancel a pending wrap
size 6x3
input "abcdef\e[0KX\r\nabcdef\e[1KY\r\nabcdef\e[2KZ"
screen
  |abcdeX|
  |     Y|
  |     Z|
cursor 6,3
ref ctlseqs: CSI Ps K (EL); xterm and tmux cancel pending wrap on EL 0, 1, and 2

=== ED 0, 1, and 2 cancel a pending wrap while ED 3 keeps it
size 6x2
input "abcdef\e[0JX\e[1;1Habcdef\e[3JY"
screen
  |abcdef|
  |Y     |
cursor 2,2
ref ctlseqs: CSI Ps J (ED); xterm and tmux cancel pending wrap on ED 0, 1, and 2, and keep it on ED 3

=== ICH, DCH, and ECH cancel a pending wrap
size 6x3
input "abcdef\e[1@X\r\nabcdef\e[1PY\r\nabcdef\e[1XZ"
screen
  |abcdeX|
  |abcdeY|
  |abcdeZ|
cursor 6,3
ref ctlseqs: CSI Ps @ (ICH), CSI Ps P (DCH), CSI Ps X (ECH)

=== Without autowrap, a wide character at the right margin is dropped
size 5x2
input "\e[?7labcd\u3042"
screen
  |abcd |
  |     |
cursor 5,1
ref ctlseqs: CSI ? 7 l (DECAWM); xterm and tmux ignore a two-cell character that does not fit at the right margin

=== LF, IND, and RI cancel a pending wrap
size 6x3
input "123456\nX\r\n123456\eMY"
screen
  |123456|
  |     Y|
  |123456|
cursor 6,2
ref xterm 409 (LF, IND, and RI move vertically from the last column and cancel pending wrap; alacritty_terminal keeps pending wrap)

=== HT at a pending wrap stays on the same row
size 6x2
input "123456\t\rX"
screen
  |X23456|
  |      |
cursor 2,1
ref xterm 409 and tmux (HT stops at the right margin without wrapping to the next row; alacritty_terminal wraps on HT)

